-- title:
--   Dyadic energy budgets for 1,024 consecutive height-two blocks
-- statement:
--   The array contains 1,024 nonnegative integers. Index \(b\) is paired with the 64 energy contributions beginning at \(64b\). Its proposed upper bound is the array entry times \(2^{-40}\). The entries were computed by rounding each exact rational block sum upwards. This definition records the data.
